1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,596
Could a valid-looking archive hide changed
bytes?

2
00:00:03,596 --> 00:00:08,000
Richard Wolff's AI-assisted adaptation
checks that boundary.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,826
Packaging reads an immutable Git commit,
not a moving working file.

4
00:00:13,826 --> 00:00:20,000
The archive contains a synthetic page,
release metadata and a manifest.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,356
Supplied expectations bind source,
context, inventory and digests.

6
00:00:26,356 --> 00:00:28,763
The valid package passes.

7
00:00:28,763 --> 00:00:33,000
This demo uses local synthetic
expectations.

8
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,784
The rehearsal substitutes payload bytes.

9
00:00:36,784 --> 00:00:42,554
It repins the outer archive hash in
evidence and expectation.

10
00:00:42,554 --> 00:00:47,000
The original per-file manifest stays
unchanged.

11
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,636
The inner payload check still rejects the
artifact.

12
00:00:51,636 --> 00:00:58,000
Outer digest agreement alone cannot prove
the intended files survived.

13
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,430
Real expectations need an independently
trusted source.

14
00:01:02,430 --> 00:01:06,215
Hashes are not signatures or CI
authentication.

15
00:01:06,215 --> 00:01:10,000
This sample performs no activation or
rollback.

16
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,630
Run Exact Artifact Demo, then inspect the
payload check in release.

17
00:01:15,630 --> 00:01:20,000
Bind delivery to independently trusted
expectations.
